{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_wc33womdcn4x3x7ivxce2qgicwhhce3my66gdh5ekwqnxb6tcyca","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. Summary of what I found and did:\n\n## Phase A — surface map (3 artifacts created)\n\n| file | content |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | `nm -D` on both `.so`s. The C TU exports **exactly one** symbol — `process_buffer`; all five helpers are `static` and correctly absent from both objects. |\n| `ERRORS.md` | **33 rejection rows** + 4 documented-UB rows, grepped from every guard, early `return`, silent default-substitution, clamp, and `fprintf(stderr,…)` in `lib.c`/`main.c`. |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | **90 configuration rows**: all 32 `flags` bit combinations + 58 targeted rows (rotate 12, compact 12, dedup 6, interleave 6, reverse 12, pipeline interactions 10) × 8 data shapes × the length classes the C special-cases. |\n\n## Real completeness gap found and fixed\n\nThe Rust crate exported **zero** C-ABI symbols — the `.so` built from it had none of the C `.so`'s symbols. I added `src/ffi.rs` with `#[no_mangle] pub unsafe extern \"C\" fn process_buffer` matching the C signature exactly, plus `crate-type = [\"lib\",\"cdylib\"]`, `libloading` dev-dep, and `forbid(unsafe_code)` → `deny` so only the FFI module opts in. The FFI wrapper also encodes the write window the C implicitly requires (`compact_runs` with `threshold == 1` grows the logical length to `2*length` — the bug that smashes `main.c`'s `uint8_t buffer[256]`).\n\n## Phases B/C/D — 130 tests, all via `dlopen`/`dlsym` on both `.so`s\n\n- **Phase B** (89 tests): every `CONFIGS.md` row, randomized with fixed seeds; compares the return value **and every byte** of the scratch buffer including past the returned length and a 96-byte guard, with an input-derived (non-constant) filler.\n- **Phase C** (24 + 14 tests): every `ERRORS.md` row asserts the *same* sentinel/message/exit status — NULL pointers, `length` 0 through `usize::MAX`, one step past every range, out-of-range flag words (`0x20`, `0x8000_0000`, `0xFFFF_FFFF`, random `u32`), `INT_MIN/MAX` modes, plus all `scanf` failures and glibc `strtoul`/`strtol` saturation-and-truncation at the CLI.\n- **Phase D**: symbol diff **empty**; suite green under the single valid feature combo, `--all-features`, default, release artifacts, and the C reference rebuilt at `-O0/-O1/-O2/-O3/-Os`; `cargo check --all-targets` clean-build gives 0 warnings.\n\n## Harness credibility check\n\n16 non-equivalent mutations injected into the Rust were **all** detected (including a wrong FFI write window → SIGABRT); the 3 undetected ones are proven semantically equivalent (e.g. interleaving 2 bytes is the identity). All sources verified byte-identical to their pre-mutation state afterwards.\n\n**No divergence was found in the translated algorithms** — `src/lib.rs` already reproduced the C faithfully, including its quirks (count written before the tail `memmove`, left-rotate for small offsets vs right for large, length growth at `threshold == 1`)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":564,"cache_read_input_tokens":214935,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":564,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9a37b61e-2eea-40bc-a926-01919fa87bad","uuid":"ff58f86c-28a5-42ed-aef3-ce85f45d37ed","timestamp":"2026-08-19T22:48:52.127Z"}
